      "title": "How this graph runs",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# CrossView Warp: generate (stage 2)\n\nThe exact graph the Hub page sends to the deployment, converted to the editor format.\n\n**The page fills in, per run**\n- *Source video* `file`: the uploaded clip\n- *Prepare clip* `aspect_ratio`, `megapixels` (0.4 or 1.0); `duration` is sent as 15 and capped at the clip, so the whole clip is used\n- *CrossView Warp*: `azimuth`, `elevation`, `distance`, `hfov`, `vertical_shift`, `keep_source_aim`, the pivot the page estimated (`pivot_override` on, `pivot_x/y/z`) and, for a move, `use_keyframes` + `keyframes` + `interp_motion`\n- *Source as reference* `prompt`: `crossview.` plus the optional text\n- *Seed* `noise_seed`\n\n**Outputs**: `crossview/result` (H3 audio), `crossview/original-audio` (the clip's own audio), `crossview/warp` (the guide).\n\nStage 1 (analyze) runs the same Prepare clip and MoGe, then *CrossView Geometry Export* instead of everything from the warp on."
      ]
    }
